\title "Bum-diddy with drop-thumb"
\subtitle "Clawhammer banjo, open G drone, 2-bar loop"
\copyright "Pattern under MIT or Apache-2.0."
\tempo 70
\tuning D4 B3 G3 D3 G4
.
// Variation on the basic bum-diddy: instead of resting on the up-
// beat of beat 1, the thumb drops to a lower string (string 4 = D3,
// the low D), giving a fuller "bum-DUM-di-dy" feel.
//   bum         = melody on string 1 (0.1, D4)
//   drop-thumb  = string 4 open (0.4, D3) — same pitch class as bum
//   di          = brush of strings 1-2-3
//   dy          = thumb on the drone string (0.5, g4)
:8 0.1 0.4 (0.1 0.2 0.3) 0.5 0.1 0.4 (0.1 0.2 0.3) 0.5 |
:8 0.1 0.4 (0.1 0.2 0.3) 0.5 0.1 0.4 (0.1 0.2 0.3) 0.5 |
